  {
    "episode_id": 96863,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96863.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "And it does seem that what you're saying is Congress does their job bit by bit if there are huge challenges. But if you start knocking, start getting things done, people say Congress is working for them, representing them, solving problems, sometimes in the bipartisan way. But most importantly, solving problems, that's the path back. That's how we sort of unravel some of this. Is that how you see it?",
