    "turn_text": "I do. I do. I think you just have to keep making the case as rights are stripped away state by state by state. You make the case as these voter suppression bills get enacted so that in Georgia, you volunteers can't even give water out to voters when they have three, four hour lines like they did in the last election. These things are so evil and they're so bad that I refuse to stop making the case. And also you have had some signaling. Senator Manchin has said he's open to a standing filibuster, which would be one way to do this. And so I just keep making the case.",
